## User Guide

### Initial Setup

1. **Power On**: Press and hold the power button
2. **WiFi Configuration**: 
   - Swipe down to access Settings
   - Tap "Configure WiFi" button
   - Connect to "T-Watch-Setup" network
   - Navigate to 192.168.4.1 in web browser
   - Select your WiFi network and enter password
3. **Username Setup**: Use the web interface to set your display name
4. **Ready to Use**: Return to home screen to begin step tracking

### Daily Operation

**Basic Navigation**:
- **Home Screen**: Central hub showing time and date
- **Step Counter**: Swipe left from home to view detailed step information
- **History**: Swipe right from home to see past 3 days
- **Leaderboard**: Swipe up from home to view rankings
- **Settings**: Swipe down from any screen

**Charging**: Connect USB-C cable when battery indicator shows low level

**Step Tracking**: Simply wear the device and walk normally - steps are automatically detected and counted

### Troubleshooting

**WiFi Connection Issues**:
- Ensure correct password entry
- Verify network supports 2.4GHz (ESP32 limitation)
- Try moving closer to router during setup

**Step Count Accuracy**:
- Wear device snugly on wrist
- Ensure normal walking motion (device detects arm swing)
- Avoid excessive arm movement that might cause false counts

**Display Issues**:
- Adjust brightness in settings if screen is too dim/bright
- Press power button to wake display if it appears off

